# Stop the ZSA Moonlander keyboard's "System Control" HID interface from being
# treated as a game controller.
#
# udev's input_id builtin tags that interface ID_INPUT_JOYSTICK=1, so
# RetroArch's `udev` joypad driver enumerates it as Pad #0 and binds it to
# player PORT 1 -- which bumps the real 8BitDo to port 2. The game reads player
# 1, so every button appears dead in-game even though RetroArch "recognized the
# 8BitDo" (it did -- on port 2). ES-DE (SDL2) tolerates the phantom, which is
# why navigation there felt fine. Surfaces after a reboot reshuffles event
# numbers so the Moonlander's phantom pad enumerates before the 8BitDo.
#
# Match only the interface that actually carries the joystick tag (VID/PID +
# ID_INPUT_JOYSTICK==1) and clear it, leaving the real keyboard/system-control
# functions intact. With no phantom joystick, the 8BitDo takes port 1.
#
# ZSA Moonlander Mark I = 3297:1969. Install to /etc/udev/rules.d/ on the HOST
# (shared /dev reaches the distrobox). See docs/controller-hotkeys.md.
ACTION=="add|change", SUBSYSTEM=="input", ATTRS{idVendor}=="3297", ATTRS{idProduct}=="1969", ENV{ID_INPUT_JOYSTICK}=="1", ENV{ID_INPUT_JOYSTICK}="0"
